    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 25%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 75%;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Sustainable Fashion</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How History Is Fashionable</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Develop an argumentative paragraph on a familiar topic or issue. Interactive: Collaborate on a group argumentative paper.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write an argumentative essay on sustainable fashion practices, providing supporting evidence (e.g., "Eco-friendly fabrics, like organic cotton and bamboo, help reduce water usage and chemical pollution.") Can contribute to a group paper on sustainable fashion trends (e.g., "By 2018, some fashion companies had already implemented recycling programs to reduce waste in their production processes.") Can help organize group ideas on why retro fashion is popular (e.g., "They have unique styles and are affordable.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 35%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Stage & Description</p></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Activities & Teacher Actions</p></th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 15%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Estimated Date and Time</p></th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b><br>Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> Display diverse images of historical fashion (e.g., 70s bell bottoms, 90s grunge) juxtaposed with modern sustainable fashion items (e.g., organic cotton dress, upcycled denim). Students jot down 2-3 words describing each image (e.g., 'vintage,' 'recycled,' 'trendy') and then share with a partner, activating prior knowledge on "fashion," "style," "retro," "sustainability."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher explicitly models sentence structures relevant to the writing task using the target grammar. For example, "In the 80s, people <b>were wearing</b> neon colors, but today, eco-friendly brands <b>are creating</b> stylish designs with recycled materials." "Before the rise of fast fashion, people <b>had adopted</b> clothes for longevity. Now, companies <b>will launch</b> more ethical collections." The teacher models the pronunciation of contrastive sounds like /v/ in "vintage" and /w/ in "wear," and stress in multisyllabic words like "sustainability" and "eco-friendly" for clarity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If we talk about 'sustainable fashion,' does it mean clothes that are expensive or clothes that are good for the environment?" (Expected answer: Good for the environment.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I say 'In the 90s, people were following minimalist trends,' am I describing a short action or something that continued for a period?" (Expected answer: Something that continued for a period.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b><br>Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short informational article or infographic titled "The Enduring Appeal of Retro: How History Inspires Sustainable Fashion." The text describes how past fashion trends (e.g., vintage, retro styles) are being revived and integrated into the sustainable fashion movement, focusing on designers creating innovative, eco-friendly collections. It will contain examples of past continuous, past perfect, and future simple tenses. (Genre: Informational text; Register: Neutral; Format: Article/Infographic excerpt).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understand and analyze written information about the evolution of fashion and sustainable practices, identifying key arguments and supporting details to prepare for writing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the primary connection the article makes between historical fashion and sustainability?" (Expected: Retro styles promote sustainability by encouraging reuse and unique designs.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students read statements and determine if they are true or false based on the text. Example: "In previous decades, the fashion industry had always prioritized eco-friendly materials." (False). "Fashion brands will continue to evolve their designs to be more sustainable in the future." (True).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> Students match key vocabulary words from the article (e.g., 'vintage,' 'recycled,' 'launch,' 'evolve,' 'trend') to their definitions or contextual examples provided.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b><br>Accuracy focus on Writing.</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Developing written accuracy in using past continuous with present simple, past perfect, and future simple, along with core vocabulary (nouns: fashion, trend, vintage, retro, style, materials, sustainability, industry, designs, environment, history, future; verbs: evolve, predict, adopt, reflect, discuss, design, create, wear, prefer, inspire, change, recycle; adjectives: sustainable, fashionable, trendy, eco-friendly, vintage, retro, stylish, unique, recycled).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Transformation:</b> Students complete sentences or transform given sentences using the target grammar and vocabulary. Provide sentences related to fashion history and sustainability. For example: "In the 90s, people ________ (wear) baggy clothes. Today, designers ________ (create) new sustainable ________ (collection)." (Answer: were wearing, are creating, collections). "Before 2015, many brands ________ (not adopt) ________ (eco-friendly) practices, but now the whole ________ (industry) ________ (evolve)." (Answer: had not adopted, eco-friendly, industry, is evolving).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Argumentative Sentence Building:</b> Give students two prompts related to the theme: "Retro fashion is a key to sustainability" or "Technology will revolutionize fashion for a greener future." Students must choose one prompt and write 2-3 argumentative sentences, ensuring they use at least one past continuous/present simple comparison, one past perfect clause, and one future simple prediction. They should integrate at least three specific vocabulary words. Example: "Many brands <b>had designed</b> wasteful products for years, but now consumers <b>are demanding</b> change, and future collections <b>will focus</b> on recycled materials."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Collaborative Paragraph Drafting & Peer Check:</b> In pairs, students choose one of their argumentative sentences from the previous activity. They then expand it into a short argumentative paragraph (4-5 sentences), providing supporting details and incorporating more target vocabulary related to "sustainable," "vintage," "trend," "materials," "environment." They then exchange their paragraph with another pair for peer-checking, focusing on clarity, grammar accuracy, and vocabulary use.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b><br>Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual Argumentative Paragraph Writing (Productive) and Group Contribution (Interactive).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Description:</b> Students will individually write an argumentative paragraph (6-8 sentences) responding to one of the following prompts, related to the scenario "Sustainable Fashion" and theme "How History Is Fashionable":</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Argue for or against the statement: 'The return of retro styles is crucial for promoting sustainability in today's fashion industry.'"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Write an argumentative paragraph on why eco-friendly materials are replacing traditional ones, considering past fashion habits and future predictions."</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Each paragraph must include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A clear topic sentence stating their argument.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">At least two supporting sentences with evidence or reasoning.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One sentence using past continuous with present simple to compare trends (e.g., "In the early 2000s, people <b>were wearing</b> low-rise jeans; today, many prefer <b>recycled</b> denim").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One sentence using past perfect for a completed action related to fashion history (e.g., "Before the sustainability movement, few brands <b>had adopted</b> ethical production methods").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">One sentence using future simple for a prediction (e.g., "Fashion trends <b>will continue to evolve</b> towards more <b>sustainable</b> practices").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">A minimum of five target vocabulary words (e.g., 'sustainable,' 'vintage,' 'evolve,' 'reflect,' 'industry,' 'designs,' 'eco-friendly').</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Additionally, students will briefly contribute their main argument and one key piece of evidence to a shared online document or whiteboard, collaborating on a collective "argumentative paper" outline about sustainable fashion trends, demonstrating their interactive writing skill.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">12-15 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation of individual writing and group contributions, plus peer assessment using a simplified rubric.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their individual argumentative paragraphs. They will also use a provided checklist to peer-assess a classmate's paragraph, focusing on the criteria below. The teacher collects both the student paragraph and the peer feedback form.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Writing):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Argument Clarity & Cohesion:</b> Is the main argument clear? Are ideas organized logically? (Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar Accuracy:</b> Correct and appropriate use of past continuous, present simple, past perfect, and future simple. (Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary Use:</b> Effective and varied use of target vocabulary (e.g., sustainable, eco-friendly, evolve, reflect, trend, retro, materials). (Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Supporting Evidence:</b> Does the paragraph provide clear supporting reasons for the argument? (Excellent / Good / Needs Improvement)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration (for group contribution):</b> Contributed meaningfully and clearly to the group outline. (Yes / Partially / No)</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students write short answers to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most challenging aspect of writing your argumentative paragraph today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Which new grammar structure (past continuous, past perfect, or future simple) do you feel most confident using in your writing now?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How effectively did I use historical examples to strengthen my argument about sustainable fashion in my writing?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What specific writing strategies (e.g., outlining, peer feedback) helped me develop my paragraph today, and how can I apply them in the future?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson to support students in developing their argumentative writing skills, particularly with the integration of target grammar and vocabulary? (e.g., "The sequence of controlled-to-semi-controlled activities seemed effective in building confidence before the final production task.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled with forming coherent arguments or correctly applying the past perfect tense in their writing? (e.g., "Perhaps providing more sentence stems for argumentative structures or a quick review of verb tense choices in context would be beneficial for some students.")</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> "In our next and final lesson (Lesson 5), we will consolidate all the skills we've practiced – listening, reading, speaking, and writing – to engage in a mediation task. You will summarize and present arguments on sustainable fashion, using your developed writing skills to explain and interpret information for a final project that showcases your understanding of how history influences fashion today."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>